-- title:
--   Stripping the p-power part of a newform's level
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$ whose $p$-torsion is residually irreducible in the sense of `ModRepIsIrreducible`: the $p$-torsion subgroup of the points of $W_{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is nontrivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodules are $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $L$ be a nonzero natural number with $p^2 \mid L$, and let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals containing $p$, every prime divisor of $L$ and every prime $q$ with $q \mid \Delta_W$. Let $g$ be a weight-$2$ cusp form on $\Gamma_0(L)$ which is a newform, i.e. a normalised eigenform (its $q$-coefficients satisfy $a_1 = 1$, multiplicativity at coprime arguments, and the two prime-power recursions according as the prime divides $L$ or not) such that no proper divisor $M \mid L$ carries a normalised eigenform of weight $2$ and level $M$ whose $\ell$-th coefficients agree with those of $g$ for all primes $\ell \nmid L$. Let $\mathfrak{m}$ be a maximal ideal of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ containing $p$, and assume that for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$ there is an algebraic integer $a$ with $a = a_\ell(g)$ in $\mathbb{C}$ and $a - a_\ell(W) \equiv 0 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}}$, where $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)$. Let $N'$ be nonzero with $N' = L/p^{v_p(L)}$. Then there are an integer $k \geq 2$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_k$ of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra `heckeAlgebra N' k S₀` of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_k(\Gamma_0(N'))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N'$, $\ell \notin S_0$ together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N'$, $q \notin S_0$, such that $p \in \mathfrak{m}_k$ and $T_\ell - a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{m}_k$ for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$.
--
--   This is the $p$-power level-stripping step of level lowering: a mod-$\mathfrak{m}$ eigensystem matching the Frobenius traces of $W$, realised by a newform of level divisible by $p^2$, is shown to occur in a Hecke algebra at the prime-to-$p$ level $N'$, at the cost of an existentially quantified and unbounded weight $k \geq 2$ (no weight optimisation is asserted). It feeds the deduction that $W$ is residually modular of level prime to $p$.
